  "notes": [
    "48 skills, each with the 1–2 weighted stats the Skills tab gives it. Single-stat skills weigh 0.2 or 0.3; two-stat skills split 0.2 + 0.1.",
    "bonusFormula holds the sheet's **level** expression, not its bonus. The sheet's bonus is ROUND(level / const.bonus_divider, 0) and the v1 SpecialitySkill shape has nowhere to put the level/bonus split — TICKET-SKL-02 introduces it, and this fragment then moves to stat_weights without the numbers changing.",
    "maxBaseLevel is 0 on every skill: the sheet has no such cap, and inventing one would put a number in the User's ruleset that nothing in the source supports.",
    "The three-letter codes are ours — the sheet addresses skills by cell. They are generated to avoid colliding with any stat abbreviation or roll code, which is what the shared flat namespace requires.",
    "Duplicate name kept deliberately (Concept 02 import note): Skinning appears twice in the sheet with different levels, so they are two records until the User merges them.",
    "Verified against Concept 02: Charm = CHA * 0.3 (11.7 at Char 39), Brewing = WIS * 0.3, Black smithing = STR * 0.2, alchemy = INT * 0.2, Trading = CHA * 0.3.",
    "One divergence from Concept 02, and the sheet wins: the page has Persuasion at Char x 0.3, the live Skills tab has Char x 0.2 + Strenght x 0.1 (Skills!D31:G31). The page's 11.7 for Persuasion is Charm's number. Worth a look before the golden fixtures pin it (TICKET-DX-04)."
  ],
